N with <inline-formula><mml:math id="M24"><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mi>W</mml:mi><mml:mrow><mml:mi>j</mml:mi><mml:mo>,</mml:mo><mml:mi>j</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>0</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula>, as the connections on the main diagonal are not present.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-35021.001"/></fig><fig id="fig2" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>New recirculation network (NRC), with one connection matrix and four layers of nodes: one input layer, one output layer, and two layers of hidden nodes.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-35021.002"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Multilayer perceptron; its hidden units layer decomposesthe input vector into main nonlinear components.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-35021.003"/></fig><fig id="fig4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Elman's hidden recurrent ANN for auto-associating purposes using the backpropagation algorithm.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-35021.004"/></fig><fig id="fig5" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Thestructure and the operators of the evolutionary algorithm GenD.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-35021.005"/></fig><fig id="fig6" position="float"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>5 &#x000d7; 2 validation protocol for theindependent identification of the spatial invariants of EEGs.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-35021.006"/></fig><fig id="fig7" position="float"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>Procedure's scheme: from the squashing phase applied to EEG signal, the TWIST phase, to the final classification phase by ANNs.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-35021.007"/></fig><fig id="fig8" position="float"><label>Figure 8</label><caption><p>The average ROC curve of the ABP performance (threshold method).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CIN2007-35021.008"/></fig><fig id="fig9" position="float"><l